### ⭐ WHEN A CRITERION IS ALREADY OWNED SOMEWHERE ELSE

> ## ⛔ CITE IT. NEVER RESTATE IT.

⚠️ **Two copies of one rule diverge, and neither looks wrong on its own** — the defect exists only
between them, and nothing reads *between* files. (`doc-structure.md` §2.3 owns this rule.)

| Instead of | Write |
|---|---|
| ⛔ repeating the rule in your words | ⭐ ⬜ *`<the file that owns it>` §N owns this — here it applies as …* |

⭐ **Name what YOUR discipline adds to it.** A citation with nothing added is a pointer with extra
steps; **a citation plus the local consequence is what makes two files one system.**

⬜ **Before shipping: for every rule you wrote, ask whether one of the seven already owns it.**

